<title>USA: Faulding gets FDA approval for Iopamidol.</title>
<headline>Faulding gets FDA approval for Iopamidol.</headline>
<dateline>ELIZABETH, N.J. 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Faulding Inc said it has received U.S. Food and Drug Administration approval to market injectable Iopamidol, a generic imaging agent that is the equivalent of Isovue.</p>
<p>Total brand revenues for the Isovue drugs totaled $320 million in 1995, Faulding said.</p>
<p>Iopamidol is indicated for imaging uses for the cardiovascular system, the excretory system and head and body, Faulding said.</p>
</text>
